 {"id":"RELEASE-TJ-002","type":"task","priority":"P0","status":"pending","title":"[P0] Hold next terminal-jail release: unresolved P1 containment failure and no published Python/release-mode artifacts","description":"Readiness sweep 2026-09-27 against terminal-jail/terminal-jail v1.2.0..origin/main (HEAD eb9dda5635ed7955b41c9b685bef52774e6a0178). Do not cut a new release until the release gate is explicitly re-evaluated. Blocking evidence: TJ-DF-027 remains status=failed, priority=P1: on fresh Debian 13.7/kernel 6.12.107 the unshare orphan-teardown test failed 3/3 and a payload survived wrapper death >15s; bwrap passed and dev kernel 7.0 passed. TJ-DF-028 remains pending, with fresh-machine ci-pass and chaos-resource failures recorded. The latest dogfood runs 10/11 are PROMISING-BUT-ROUGH, not SHIPPABLE; run 11 also records that metrics are structurally zero, custom packs have no install path, and pack schema is undocumented (TJ-DF-033..035 pending). Release surface: v1.2.0 has a GitHub Release object but 0 assets; README says release-mode installs have no published assets, and no PyPI publishing workflow/artifact channel was found, matching TJ-DF-032 unresolved channel finding. No RELEASE-cut authorization row exists. Evidence: CI run 36289593520 is green on HEAD eb9dda5; latest range includes 63 commits and one feat (conventional-prefix count 1 feat, 5 fix; 0 breaking markers; remaining history largely merge/board/docs/test/dogfood). Candidate bump if blockers close and authorization is granted: v1.3.0 (minor), not released by this row. Acceptance: close or explicitly disposition TJ-DF-027/028 and relevant dogfood release blockers; decide and document supported package/artifact channel (including usable release assets if release mode is advertised); obtain separate explicit RELEASE-cut authorization; then run all release gates on exact proposed tag SHA. Do not tag or publish as part of this task.","created_at":"2026-09-27T01:39:41-05:00","created_by":"releng-satel